course: dictionary
lesson: 12138
title: Shared words: communal
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Communal means shared by everyone in a group, or done by a group together. Look at the words around it to find its meaning. «The flats have a communal garden where everyone can play.» The garden belongs to all the flats, not just one family, so communal means shared.
explain: «The class enjoyed a communal lunch, with everyone sharing food at long tables.» The words sharing and everyone are clues. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning, shared or done together, and check the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Communal means shared by all the people in a group or building.
fact: Communal also means done by or involving a group of people together.
fact: «A communal kitchen» is one kitchen that everyone uses.
fact: «Communal» can also describe things to do with different communities, such as tensions between groups in the news.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The flats have a communal laundry in the basement.» What does communal mean here? | Only for one family | Very dirty | Closed all year | *Shared by all the people in the flats
exercise: «We ate a communal meal together at the church hall.» What does communal suggest? | Eaten alone in silence | Eaten very quickly by one person | *Done together by a group | Cooked by a robot
exercise: «Everyone in the club uses the communal kitchen.» Which word from this sentence means shared by all? | kitchen | club | everyone | *communal
test: «The school trip had communal showers and one big dormitory.» Which meaning fits communal here? | Very cold | *Shared by everyone on the trip | Made of stone | Locked and private
test: «Our village held a communal singing evening, and everyone joined in.» What does communal mean here? | *Done together by a group | Sold for money | Quiet and private | Done by one person alone
exam: Ella asks, «Is a communal garden only for one flat?» What is the answer? | Yes, it is closed to everybody | No, it is a shop | *No, it is shared by everyone who lives there | Yes, it belongs to one flat only
